# The build context of Dockerfile.gotest alone. BuildKit reads a
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the one at the repository root, so
# this widens the context for this build without touching the root file, whose
# deny-all keeps the four image contexts down to install.sh.
#
# Nested re-inclusion needs every level spelled out: an exception cannot reach
# into a folder the line above excluded, so services/ is let back in before its
# children are filtered.
*
!Dockerfile.gotest
!go.work
!go.work.sum
!pkg
!tools
!tests
!services
services/*
!services/dispat

# The export folder of a previous build: output rather than source, and it
# would grow the context with every build.
services/dispat/dist

# What the dispat suite reads beyond its module: the installers and image
# folders the selfupdate tests hold to the CLI's asset names, and the
# architecture page the plan tests hold the diagnostic codes to.
!install.sh
!install.ps1
!docker
!specs
specs/*
!specs/ccme-spec
!specs/ccme-spec/SPEC.md
!specs/ccme-spec/*.sh
specs/ccme-spec/.ccme-version.*
!specs/agent-guide
specs/agent-guide/*
!specs/agent-guide/*.sh
!packages
packages/*
!packages/cli
packages/cli/*
!packages/cli/dispat.yaml
!packages/docs
packages/docs/*
!packages/docs/dispat.yaml
!packages/docs/docs
!packages/docs/demo
packages/docs/demo/illustration/node_modules
packages/docs/demo/illustration/out

# The profiles and logs a suite run left behind, for the badge and report
# targets, and the release experiments' records beside them: those run against
# a registry a container is allowed to break, so they reach a build through
# the context rather than from a stage. The binary covdata folder stays out:
# integration.out is its already-condensed form, and only the test-integration
# stage in here writes or reads the raw counters.
!coverage
coverage/covdata

# The shell sweep's inputs. Shell files only: scripts/ also holds a python
# renderer and services/dispat/announce holds shared fonts and each channel's
# audio. Include only the publisher scripts, the shared cross-posting, and each
# channel's configuration, card and copy needed by tests.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/*.sh
!scripts/announce-test.py
services/dispat/announce/*
!services/dispat/announce/*.sh
!services/dispat/announce/publish.yaml
!services/dispat/announce/rc
services/dispat/announce/rc/*
!services/dispat/announce/rc/announcement.md
!services/dispat/announce/rc/crier.yaml
!services/dispat/announce/rc/links.md
!services/dispat/announce/rc/template.html
!services/dispat/announce/stable
services/dispat/announce/stable/*
!services/dispat/announce/stable/announcement.md
!services/dispat/announce/stable/crier.yaml
!services/dispat/announce/stable/links.md
!services/dispat/announce/stable/template.html

# Bootstrap integration fixture and pinned tool policy.
!.aqua
!scripts/test-install-tools.py

# The configuration sweep's inputs: every committed dispat config, whose
# `scripts` entries are shell like anything else the sweep reads, and the
# reader that pulls them out. The configs under pkg/, docker/, tools/ and
# tests/ arrive with those folders; the rest are named here one by one,
# because each sits in a folder an exception above has already filtered. A
# new package whose folder is filtered belongs on this list, or its scripts
# become the only shell in the repository nothing checks.
!scripts/lint-config-scripts.py
!dispat.yaml
!packages/dispat.yaml
!services/dispat.yaml
!specs/agent-guide/dispat.yaml
!specs/ccme-spec/dispat.yaml
!infra
infra/*
!infra/dispat.yaml
